course: dictionary
lesson: 13935
title: Lengthy and long
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Lengthy is an adjective, so it describes a noun. It means very long, and often too long, in time or in words. «We had a lengthy wait for the bus.» The word wait tells you what is long: the time you spent waiting.
explain: «The teacher's instructions were lengthy, and by the end we had forgotten the first step.» The clue is forgotten the first step. Lengthy here means the instructions went on so long that they were tiring. Swap in long and check: the sentence still makes sense, but lengthy tells you it was too much.
explain: Lengthy can also describe writing. «Her report was lengthy, with twenty pages to read.» Twenty pages is the clue. Always ask: what is long here, the time or the words? Then try very long in the sentence and see if it still fits.
fact: Lengthy means very long, often too long.
fact: It can be about time, as in «a lengthy wait».
fact: It can be about words or pages, as in «a lengthy report».
fact: Lengthy often suggests that the length is tiring or boring.
fact: Long is a simpler word that often fits in the same place, but lengthy sounds more formal.
exercise: «The film was lengthy, and we kept looking at the clock.» What does lengthy mean? | Very short | Very funny | Very loud | *Very long
exercise: «We had a lengthy wait for the bus in the rain.» Find and copy one word that tells you the wait was long. | *lengthy | bus | rain | we
exercise: Mum says, «The forms are lengthy.» What does she mean? | They are very small | *They take a long time to fill in | They are written in bright colours | They are free to take home
test: «The lengthy speech made everyone yawn.» What made everyone yawn? | *The speech was too long | The speech was very loud | The room was too hot | The speech was very funny
test: Which word is closest in meaning to lengthy? | *long | short | loud | quick
exam: Which word means the opposite of lengthy? | *Brief | Lengthy | Long | Enormous
